    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493338290/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Friday, Nov. 20, 1908
Somerset Hotel, Boston.
Miss Elizabeth Sargent came to see me at 11, earlier Miss Moffat came, chattering unchanged.
Bernnhard lunched with Dr. Marks and met that interesting Dr. Prince of the “Dissociated Personalities”  studies . I lunched at Miss Yerzas’, very dull.
We consoled ourselves with dining again at the dear Wilsons. They had in a pretty red-haired woman to sing.
I forget to say we had tea with the  Peannains . Their son is engaged to Brush’s daughter. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 347 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1908> .

